    "created_at": "2016-03-18T16:27:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-18T16:27:37Z",
    "body": "I'd like to open talks with the SVGWG about this case, script, and style, since it sounds like they are all similar. I'd want them to be comfortable with whatever decision on who maintains the spec, how namespaces are handled, and how element interfaces are handled.\n\nHowever `<image>` doesn't seem like `<img>` to me at all. See https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG2/embedded.html#ImageElement. It uses `href` instead of `src` and isn't a void element (it contains a lot of different things). It has a (case-sensitive?) `preserveAspectRatio` attribute. And it inherits from `SVGGraphicsElement`. Not great.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
