    "created_at": "2016-03-23T10:45:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-23T10:45:46Z",
    "body": "Yeah I didn't mean dropping support for svg:image, just treat it as legacy and not bother trying to add support for srcset/picture with svg:image -- if you want new features use html:img instead. I think it doesn't make much sense to have this:\n\n```\n<svg:svg ...>\n <html:picture>\n  <html:source srcset=\"...\"/>\n  <svg:image href=\"...\" srcset=\"...\"/>\n </html:picture>\n ...\n```\n\nDoes SVG have some features that svg:image currently has but html:img doesn't that are necessary in SVG?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
